          "filename": "140607-A-ON889-86 (14189120997).jpg",
          "caption": "PORTSMOUTH, VIRGINIA -- Colonel Paul Olsen, Norfolk District commander, thanks Clean the Bay Day organizer Program Analyst Ella Skeeter-Webster June 7, 2014 at the Craney Island Dredged Material Management Area. Approximately 69 volunteers participated in this year’s event and more than 1,410 pounds of bagged trash and 540 pounds of bulk items were collected. Organizations represented included not only the Norfolk District but also members from Lafayette, Woodside, I.C. Norcom and Churchland High Schools, Girls Scout Troup 1381, Bayside Area Boy Scouts, Boy Scout Troup 6, Norfolk State University, Old Dominion University, Army, Navy, U.S. Coast Guard, the Society of Military Engineers and other organizations not captured. A total of 68 bags of trash - 1,410 pounds of bagged trash and approximately 590 pounds of bulk non-bagged items – were collected. Approximately 69 volunteers participated in this year’s event and more than 1,410 pounds of bagged trash and 540 pounds of bulk items were collected. (U.S. Army photo/Pamela k Spaugy)",
